title PN model for NGC 650
set save prefix "pn_ngc650"
# model of the torus of the PN NGC 650
#
# commands controlling continuum =========
table star Rauch H-Ca solar 5.317493 log 8.000000
luminosity 35.994549 log range -7.999566 6.866524
cmb
#
# commands for density & abundances =========
hden 2.139592 log
constant density
abundances planetary no grains
element helium abundance -0.96 log
element carbon abundance -3.06 log
element nitrogen abundance -3.80 log
element oxygen abundance -3.38 log
element neon abundance -4.03 log
element magnesium abundance -5.40 log
element silicon abundance -5.44 log
element phosphorus abundance -6.59 log
element sulphur abundance -5.21 log
element chlorine abundance -7.08 log
element argon abundance -5.63 log
grain abund 0.425984 log "graphite_0m100.opc"
#
# commands controlling geometry  =========
radius 17.455679 LOG
cylinder semi-height 17.474 log
sphere
stop temperature off
stop continuum flux at 350 micron 0.62 jansky
#
# other commands for details     =========
cosmic rays background
distance 1200 linear parsec
iterate
set nFnu add 60 micron
set nFnu add 100 micron
set nFnu add 160 micron
set nFnu add 250 micron
set nFnu add 500 micron
set nFnu add 6.181 cm
set nFnu add 21.41 cm
# include dust/radio emission both from the near and far side of the torus
set nFnu diffuse inward, diffuse outward
#
# commands controlling output    =========
print line flux seen at earth
print line sort wavelength
normalize to "H  1" 4861.32 scale factor 100
save continuum last units micron ".con"
save physical conditions ".phy"
save monitors last ".asr"
save grain temperature last ".grntem"
#
# commands giving the asserts    =========
monitor  "He 2"  1640.41A vacuum  -10.2343 line intensity
monitor  "C  3"  1906.68A vacuum  -10.1220 line intensity
monitor  "C  3"  1908.73A vacuum  -10.3029 line intensity
monitor  "Ne 4"  2421.66A air     -11.6768 line intensity
monitor  "Ne 4"  2424.28A air     -11.5103 line intensity
monitor  "Mg 2"  2795.53A air     -11.9021 line intensity
monitor  "Mg 2"  2802.71A air     -12.1963 line intensity
monitor  "Ar 4"  4740.12A air     -12.5788 line intensity
monitor  "O  3"  5006.84A air      -9.7851 line intensity
monitor  "N  1"  5197.90A air     -12.0010 line intensity
monitor  "N  1"  5200.26A air     -11.8853 line intensity
monitor  "Cl 3"  5517.71A air     -12.9014 line intensity
monitor  "S  2"  6716.44A air     -10.9872 line intensity
monitor  "S  2"  6730.82A air     -11.0916 line intensity
monitor  "He 1"  7065.18A air     -12.8631 line intensity
monitor  "S  3"  9530.62A air     -10.9011 line intensity
monitor  "Ar 5"  13.0985m air     -12.7869 line intensity
monitor  "Ne 3"  15.5509m air     -10.8201 line intensity
monitor  "P  3"  17.8797m air     -12.9386 line intensity
monitor  "O  4"  25.8863m air     -10.2711 line intensity
monitor  "Si 2"  34.8046m air     -11.5949 line intensity
monitor  "nFnu"  60.0000m vacuum   -9.5592 line intensity
monitor  "nFnu"  100.000m vacuum   -9.5896 line intensity
monitor  "nFnu"  160.000m vacuum  -10.0272 line intensity
monitor  "nFnu"  250.000m vacuum  -10.7094 line intensity
monitor  "nFnu"  350.000m vacuum  -11.2721 line intensity
monitor  "nFnu"  500.000m vacuum  -11.8539 line intensity
monitor  "nFnu"  6.18100c vacuum  -14.2427 line intensity
monitor  "nFnu"  21.4100c vacuum  -14.7293 line intensity
#
# pn_ngc650.in
# class pn
# ========================================
# 

NGC 650 is a carbon-rich bipolar PN where the dominant feature is
the equatorial density enhancement or torus, which is what this
model is trying to reproduce using the cylinder command. The gas
abundances and grains are fairly typical for a type IIa C-rich
PN. The model is set up to stop when the FIR flux observed with
Herschel PACS and SPIRE is reached, which happens to be roughly
at the ionization front.

This is a slightly modified version of the model that has been
published in van Hoof et al. (2013)
https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2013A%26A...560A...7V/abstract
